<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arung Matoa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arung Matoa, roughly &quot;chief lord&quot; in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bugis">Bugis</a>, was the title of the head of the Bugis kingdom of Wajo in South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulawesi">Sulawesi</a>. Unlike most neighbouring rulers, the Arung Matoa did not inherit the office but was elected by a council of nobles, who could also remove him. The office lasted from the 15th century until Wajo was absorbed into the Indonesian state in the mid-20th century.</p></div>
